1
00:00:01,150 --> 00:00:05,150
<i>Deep beneath the mountain,</i>
<i>where the sun had never shone...</i>

2
00:00:05,150 --> 00:00:07,679
<i>walked a warrior named Anger.</i>

3
00:00:07,850 --> 00:00:12,916
<i>He was a man of very few words...</i>
<i>and even fewer smiles.</i>

4
00:00:13,440 --> 00:00:17,650
<i>When vines blocked his path,</i>
<i>he did not go around.</i>

5
00:00:20,350 --> 00:00:24,489
<i>Cobwebs, he swept aside</i>
<i>with the back of his hand.</i>

6
00:00:25,850 --> 00:00:30,012
<i>At the end of the tunnel</i>
<i>stood an old iron door.</i>

7
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:33,730
<i>It was locked.</i>

8
00:00:33,750 --> 00:00:37,306
<i>Anger did not believe</i>
<i>in locked doors.</i>

9
00:00:38,850 --> 00:00:41,360
<i>Only in open ones.</i>

10
00:00:41,650 --> 00:00:44,890
<i>Beyond the door lay</i>
<i>a cavern so vast,</i>

11
00:00:44,890 --> 00:00:48,190
<i>his torchlight could</i>
<i>not find its walls.</i>

12
00:00:48,250 --> 00:00:52,555
<i>It was dark, and cold,</i>
<i>and very, very quiet.</i>

13
00:00:55,150 --> 00:01:00,240
<i>He did not see the eyes.</i>
<i>But the eyes... had seen him.</i>

14
00:01:03,250 --> 00:01:06,030
<i>And then, there</i>
<i>was only darkness.</i>

15
00:01:06,050 --> 00:01:09,737
<i>Anger stood perfectly</i>
<i>still... and listened.</i>

16
00:01:11,550 --> 00:01:15,030
<i>Nothing. Nothing he could see.</i>

17
00:01:15,050 --> 00:01:17,910
<i>So he pressed on, sword raised...</i>

18
00:01:17,910 --> 00:01:22,149
<i>never noticing the thin cracks</i>
<i>spreading beneath his feet.</i>

19
00:01:24,150 --> 00:01:30,132
<i>He caught the edge. But steel is</i>
<i>heavy... and stone is unforgiving.</i>

20
00:01:30,250 --> 00:01:32,530
<i>Anger did not scream.</i>

21
00:01:32,550 --> 00:01:35,119
<i>He simply closed his eyes.</i>

22
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:37,880
<i>His sword bit into the stone...</i>

23
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:40,528
<i>...until it struck solid rock.</i>

24
00:01:47,050 --> 00:01:51,914
<i>The sword had saved his</i>
<i>life. But not his bones.</i>

25
00:01:53,714 --> 00:01:55,998
<i>And he was not alone.</i>

26
00:01:57,014 --> 00:01:59,559
<i>Then the darkness took him.</i>

27
00:02:02,114 --> 00:02:05,634
<i>When he woke...</i>
<i>he could move only one arm.</i>

28
00:02:06,434 --> 00:02:11,892
<i>The creature had waited a very</i>
<i>long time for a meal like this.</i>

29
00:02:19,392 --> 00:02:22,139
<i>Someone... had thrown that rock.</i>

30
00:02:22,339 --> 00:02:24,749
You gotta watch
out for those things.

31
00:02:24,749 --> 00:02:27,049
They'll make you their lunch.

32
00:02:27,249 --> 00:02:29,989
But I'm gonna make
it MY lunch now.

33
00:02:32,489 --> 00:02:36,437
<i>Anger had no idea</i>
<i>how to feel about this.</i>

34
00:02:36,689 --> 00:02:41,369
<i>With great effort, Anger dragged</i>
<i>himself up against the wall.</i>

35
00:02:41,389 --> 00:02:47,359
Who... are you?
How did you get here?

36
00:02:49,459 --> 00:02:55,749
The food was good... but now
a nap sounds even better.

37
00:02:55,769 --> 00:02:58,160
<i>Anger rolled his eyes.</i>

38
00:03:00,260 --> 00:03:04,165
<i>Within seconds,</i>
<i>the stranger was snoring.</i>

39
00:03:04,185 --> 00:03:06,625
<i>Anger stared into the darkness,</i>

40
00:03:06,625 --> 00:03:09,810
<i>and wondered where</i>
<i>his life had gone wrong.</i>

41
00:03:09,910 --> 00:03:14,190
How did I get myself into this...

42
00:03:14,690 --> 00:03:18,507
<i>Eventually, he gave up...</i>
<i>and went to sleep.</i>

43
00:03:20,107 --> 00:03:22,545
<i>He did not sleep for long.</i>

44
00:03:25,107 --> 00:03:29,626
<i>Something warm... and wet...</i>
<i>was dripping on his face.</i>

45
00:03:33,226 --> 00:03:35,676
What the hell are you?!

46
00:03:35,976 --> 00:03:40,966
That's my friend. He's saying hi.
I think he likes you.

47
00:03:40,986 --> 00:03:44,518
<i>Anger shuffled out</i>
<i>from under the drool.</i>

48
00:03:44,618 --> 00:03:49,508
Tell your friend to give
me a little space. Please.

49
00:03:49,708 --> 00:03:52,693
<i>The creature did not like that.</i>

50
00:03:56,093 --> 00:04:00,533
Hey, he can hear you, buddy.
Treat him with some respect.

51
00:04:00,533 --> 00:04:02,623
We go way back, okay?

52
00:04:02,643 --> 00:04:05,890
<i>Anger wiped the</i>
<i>slobber from his face.</i>

53
00:04:08,390 --> 00:04:12,636
<i>No one said anything...</i>
<i>for a very long time.</i>

54
00:04:12,790 --> 00:04:17,680
Well. How are you guys
gonna get out of here?

55
00:04:17,700 --> 00:04:26,476
(laughs for way too long)

56
00:04:26,576 --> 00:04:30,786
We would've gotten out of here
a long time ago if we could have.

57
00:04:30,786 --> 00:04:33,776
But now it seems you're
stuck in here with us.

58
00:04:33,776 --> 00:04:35,986
How do you feel about that?

59
00:04:36,686 --> 00:04:40,506
Well... I guess I'll die then.

60
00:04:45,106 --> 00:04:49,209
<i>For one brief moment,</i>
<i>Anger had almost smiled.</i>

61
00:04:49,609 --> 00:04:55,056
<i>And so began the strangest</i>
<i>friendship the deep had ever known.</i>
